  "notes": "Downloaded directly via BEA's public regional-data ZIP endpoint (no API key required): https://apps.bea.gov/regional/zip/SARPP.zip (table SARPP, 'Regional price parities by state', covering 2008-2024). This is a full, un-truncated primary-source CSV (BEA does not block direct curl/wget downloads of these bulk ZIP files, unlike BLS's xlsx endpoints). RPPs are an INDEX where the U.S. national average = 100 for every year (not a dollar amount); a state RPP of 110 means prices there average 10% above the U.S. average that year. LINE CODE MAPPING (BEA's own SARPP table definitions): LineCode 1 = 'All items' (all_items); LineCode 2 = 'Goods' (durable+nondurable consumption goods: apparel, education, food, housing, medical, recreation, transportation, other goods) (goods); LineCode 3 = 'Services: Housing' -- BEA states this line is estimated ONLY for tenant-occupied housing rents plus an imputed rental value for owner-occupied housing, i.e. this is effectively a RENTS index, not an owner cash-outlay index (services_housing_rents); LineCode 4 = 'Services: Utilities' (water/sanitation + electricity/gas) (services_utilities); LineCode 5 = 'Services: Other' (all other services except rents: education, food, medical, recreation, transportation, other) (services_other). Both 2024 (latest published) and 2023 (prior vintage, per task spec's 'ideally also 2023 vintage' request) values are included per geography as suffixed fields (_2024 / _2023). 'US' row (geo='US', geo_name='United States') is the national baseline = 100.000 for every year by construction. Washington DC is included as geo='DC'. No dollar-denominated cost-of-living figures are available from BEA RPP -- this is purely a relative price-level index; the v2 frontend must combine this with a dollar anchor (e.g. national mean expenditure from BLS CES) to derive dollar estimates by state, matching the same limitation documented for BEA national income data in v1's data/README.md (BEA publishes no dollar thresholds, shares/indices only)."
